-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/d1f0a53f-959c-40bf-8b65-f87d86816e46
-- title:
--   Posterior weights and replica averages for a finite signal observed through a kernel
-- statement:
--   Let a finite signal $\theta\in\Theta$ have prior $\pi$ and be observed through a Markov kernel $\kappa$ into a measurable space $O$, and let $\nu=\int\kappa_\theta\,\pi(d\theta)$ be the law of the observation. The posterior weight of $\theta$ at an observation $o$ is
--
--   $$P(\theta\mid o)=\pi\{\theta\}\,\frac{d\kappa_\theta}{d\nu}(o),$$
--
--   and the posterior average of $m$ independent replicas is $\langle g(\sigma^1,\dots,\sigma^m)\rangle_o=\sum_{\sigma\in\Theta^m}\prod_jP(\sigma^j\mid o)\,g(\sigma)$.
--
--   This is the general setting of the Nishimori identity (Lemma 3.1), which the paper uses both for the Gaussian model and along the revealing path, where the retained observations include revealed coordinates of $\theta$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The density is a Radon–Nikodym derivative; $\kappa_\theta\ll\nu$ whenever $\pi\{\theta\}>0$.
-- source:
--   Z. Li, Efficient Posterior Sampling for ℤ₂ Synchronization, arXiv:2610.08199 (held version, sha256 536ad4d8…), Lemma 3.1, p.14

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped ENNReal
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace Z2PostSamp

noncomputable section

/-!
# Posterior weights and replica averages for a finite signal observed through a kernel

Z. Li, *Efficient Posterior Sampling for ℤ₂ Synchronization*, arXiv:2610.08199 (held version,
sha256 536ad4d8…), Lemma 3.1, p.14: "Let `ℱ` be the sigma-field generated by the observations being
retained. Conditional on `ℱ`, let `σ¹, …, σ^{a+1}` be independent samples from `ℒ(θ | ℱ)`".

**Formalization Note.** A finite signal `θ ∈ Θ` with prior `π` is observed through a Markov kernel
`κ : Θ → O` (the retained observations; they may include revealed coordinates of `θ`). With the
marginal `ν = κ ∘ₘ π` of the observation, the posterior weight of `θ` at `o` is
`π{θ} · (dκ_θ/dν)(o)` (Bayes' formula with a Radon–Nikodym density; `κ_θ ≪ ν` whenever `π{θ} > 0`).
`postAvg` is the posterior average `⟨g(σ¹, …, σ^m)⟩` of `m` independent replicas.
-/

/-- The posterior weight `P(θ | o) = π{θ} · (dκ_θ/dν)(o)`, `ν = κ ∘ₘ π`. -/
def postWeight {Θ O : Type} [MeasurableSpace Θ] [MeasurableSpace O] (π : Measure Θ)
    (κ : Kernel Θ O) (o : O) (θ : Θ) : ℝ :=
  (π {θ}).toReal * ((κ θ).rnDeriv (κ ∘ₘ π) o).toReal

/-- The posterior average `⟨g(σ¹, …, σ^m)⟩` of `m` independent posterior replicas at `o`. -/
def postAvg {Θ O : Type} [Fintype Θ] [DecidableEq Θ] [MeasurableSpace Θ] [MeasurableSpace O]
    (π : Measure Θ) (κ : Kernel Θ O) (m : ℕ) (o : O) (g : (Fin m → Θ) → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ σ : Fin m → Θ, (∏ j, postWeight π κ o (σ j)) * g σ

end

end Z2PostSamp


